  "reasoning": "The claim is demonstrably false. The Great Wall of China is not visible to the naked human eye from low Earth orbit, let alone further out in space. Averaging only about 6 to 9 meters in width and constructed from local stone and soil that blends into the surrounding landscape, it lacks the optical contrast and angular size necessary for human visual resolution from orbit. Astronauts from NASA and China's space program (such as Yang Liwei in 2003) have repeatedly confirmed it cannot be identified with the unaided eye, whereas other human-made features like highways, canals, and city lights are easily discernible.",
